# Line endings.
#
# Git for Windows ships core.autocrlf=true in its system config, so without
# this file a Windows clone rewrites every tracked text file to CRLF on
# checkout. Two consequences, both measured on a clean clone (issue #27):
#
#  1. `tools/sync_plugin.py --check` byte-compares content generated in memory
#     (LF) against the file on disk (CRLF) and can never match, so it reports
#     false drift. That is a standing gate per CLAUDE.md §2/§4 which no Windows
#     contributor could satisfy.
#  2. Worse, autocrlf's binary detection only samples for NUL bytes, so a small
#     PDF with no NUL early in the file is treated as text and CORRUPTED on
#     checkout: tekton-eval-kit/Tekton-Eval-Kit-Instructions.pdf arrived as
#     11,148 bytes against a stored 11,012 — 136 bytes of CRLF expansion. git
#     status hid it, because it normalised the file again on compare.
#
# Normalise text to LF in the repository AND in the working tree on every
# platform. macOS and Linux see no change; Windows stops seeing false drift and
# stops corrupting binaries.
* text=auto eol=lf

# --- binary: never convert these bytes ---------------------------------------
# Do not rely on content sniffing. Revit containers in particular are the
# product's deliverable format and are byte-compared against sha256 pins in
# src/rvt/frontdoor/assets/genesis_base.json.
*.rvt   binary
*.rfa   binary
*.rte   binary
*.rft   binary
*.zip   binary
*.gz    binary
*.bin   binary
*.pdf   binary
*.png   binary
*.jpg   binary
*.jpeg  binary
*.ico   binary

# --- exempt from renormalisation ---------------------------------------------
# The only tracked text blobs that already store CRLF. Listed file-by-file
# rather than by directory so that adding this file changes no stored content:
# a directory-wide -text would have captured LF-stored siblings and committed
# the CRLF-polluted working-tree copies of them instead.
#
# Vendored third-party source — upstream's bytes, not ours to reformat.
**/_vendor/olefile/olefile.py        -text
**/_vendor/olefile/LICENSE.txt       -text
**/_vendor/olefile/CONTRIBUTORS.txt  -text
# Revit shared-parameter files are a Revit-side interchange format; leave the
# bytes exactly as Revit wrote them.
*shared-parameters.txt               -text

# --- always LF regardless of the above ---------------------------------------
*.sh    text eol=lf
